  "text_md": "100\n\n![](<e3b1c4a529f268686b0f03accb2b91604ef3_pg10_images/imageFile1.png>)\n\n90\n\n80\n\n70\n\n60\n\n50\n\n5-6 years\n\n40\n\n30\n\n6-7 years\n\n20\n\n7-8 years\n\n10\n\nCommon cause\n\nABC\n\nACB\n\nCommon cause\n\nABC\n\nACB\n\ncausal\n\ncause\n\ncausal\n\ncausal\n\ncause\n\ncausal\n\nchain\n\nchain\n\nchain\n\nchain\n\nCausal chain\n\nCommon cause\n\nFig. 2. Percentage of response choices for each causal structure as a function of age group. Correct responses to the causal chain are denoted as ABC.\n\nTable 1 Percentage of times that participants chose each intervention collapsed across common cause and causal chain trials.\n\n<table>\n  <tr>\n    <th> </th>\n    <th colspan=\"6\">Informative</th>\n    <th colspan=\"3\">Uninformative</th>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td> </td>\n    <td>B+</td>\n    <td>A–B+</td>\n    <td> </td>\n    <td>A–C+</td>\n    <td>A+C–</td>\n    <td>A+B–</td>\n    <td>A+</td>\n    <td>B–C+</td>\n    <td>B+C–</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td>5–6 years</td>\n    <td>17.9</td>\n    <td>9.5</td>\n    <td>C+ 12.9</td>\n    <td>5.1</td>\n    <td>9.6</td>\n    <td>8.3</td>\n    <td>23.3</td>\n    <td>8.2</td>\n    <td>5.4</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td>6-7 years</td>\n    <td>17.5</td>\n    <td>9.2</td>\n    <td>14.2 9.4</td>\n    <td>8.2</td>\n    <td>8.2</td>\n    <td>9.0</td>\n    <td>21.8</td>\n    <td>6.4</td>\n    <td>5.6</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td>7-8 years</td>\n    <td>10.8</td>\n    <td>11.3</td>\n    <td>9.4</td>\n    <td>11.1</td>\n    <td>14.8</td>\n    <td>13.5</td>\n    <td>14.2</td>\n    <td>6.9</td>\n    <td>8.0</td>\n  </tr>\n</table>\n\n\nTable 2 Regression analyses from Experiment 1.\n\n<table>\n  <tr>\n    <th>Dependent</th>\n    <th>Parameter</th>\n    <th>Estimate</th>\n    <th>SE</th>\n    <th>Odds ratio</th>\n    <th> </th>\n    <th>p (>| z |)</th>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td rowspan=\"2\">P correct (chain)</td>\n    <td>Intercept</td>\n    <td> </td>\n    <td>1.80</td>\n    <td> </td>\n    <td>z –2.65</td>\n    <td>008</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td>% Informative</td>\n    <td>7.37</td>\n    <td>2.70</td>\n    <td>1587</td>\n    <td>2.73</td>\n    <td>006</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td rowspan=\"2\">P correct (common</td>\n    <td>Intercept</td>\n    <td>1.87</td>\n    <td>1.48</td>\n    <td> </td>\n    <td>1.27</td>\n    <td>.21</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td>% Informative</td>\n    <td> </td>\n    <td>2.15</td>\n    <td>0.267</td>\n    <td> </td>\n    <td>.54</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td rowspan=\"2\">P correct (chain)</td>\n    <td>Intercept</td>\n    <td>20.81</td>\n    <td>0.75</td>\n    <td> </td>\n    <td> </td>\n    <td>.278</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td>Efficiency</td>\n    <td>1.22</td>\n    <td>0.92</td>\n    <td>3.39</td>\n    <td>1.32</td>\n    <td>.186</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td rowspan=\"2\">P correct (common</td>\n    <td>Intercept</td>\n    <td>3.39</td>\n    <td>0.99</td>\n    <td> </td>\n    <td>3.39</td>\n    <td>0007</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td> </td>\n    <td>~3.31</td>\n    <td>1.27</td>\n    <td>0.037</td>\n    <td>–2.62</td>\n    <td>.009</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td rowspan=\"2\">P correct (chain)</td>\n    <td>Intercept</td>\n    <td> </td>\n    <td>1.74</td>\n    <td> </td>\n    <td>2.53</td>\n    <td>012</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td>Quality</td>\n    <td>7.98</td>\n    <td>3.06</td>\n    <td>2921</td>\n    <td>2.61</td>\n    <td>009</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td rowspan=\"2\">P correct (common</td>\n    <td>Intercept</td>\n    <td>1.46</td>\n    <td>1.40</td>\n    <td> </td>\n    <td>1.04</td>\n    <td>30</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td>Quality</td>\n    <td>20.78</td>\n    <td>2.24</td>\n    <td>0.46</td>\n    <td>~0.35</td>\n    <td>73</td>\n  </tr>\n</table>\n\n\nNote: The table shows three separate analyses of predictors of performance on the causal chain and common cause trials: percentage informative interventions, efﬁciency, and intervention quality. * p < .05.\n\n** p < .01.\n\np < .001.\n\np < .001.\n\n",
